Body:
> +1 to runtime-level tool restriction. My use case: Plan mode should be a true read-only mode where the model physically cannot call edit/write/create tools — not just prompted not to. The same hard block would also make a dedicated "Ask" mode (like Cursor's) possible.

The tool itself is capable of doing this, it just needs a working default configuration with this block in the default `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json`:

`
  "agent": {
    "plan": {
      "permission": {
        "bash": {
          "*": "ask"
        }
      }
    }
  }
`

We encountered exactly this. Beyond the `sessionID` crash: in some OpenCode builds, `chat.message` doesn't fire at all — the `trigger("chat.message", ...)` call site is missing from the session processor entirely. We loaded a plugin with a `chat.message` hook, the plugin loaded without errors ("loading plugin" in logs), but the hook was never called.

**Workaround: use the `event` hook instead.** Listen for `message.part.updated` bus events:

```js
event: async ({ event }) => {
  if (event.type === "message.part.updated") {
    const text = event.properties.part.text
    // text has the full part content for TextPart/ReasoningPart
  }
}
```

Also: Bun's `fetch()` ignores `tls: { rejectUnauthorized: false }`. Use `new https.Agent({ rejectUnauthorized: false })` from `node:https` for plugins calling HTTPS endpoints with self-signed certs.

Related: #22831 (feature request to expose body to chat.message), #29022 (our findings)
